<title>USA: Guess moves most US manufacturing to Mex - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Guess moves most US manufacturing to Mex - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guess? Inc, long one of the biggest clothing manufacturers in Los Angeles, is quietly moving most of its U.S. manufacturing to Mexico and other countries south of the border, The Wall Street Journal reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>The company, dogged by allegations of illegal labor practices, will sew 35 percent of its garments in Los Angeles next month, down from 75 percent five months ago, the story said.</p>
<p>The Journal quotes Guess Chief Executive Maurice Marciano as saying the shift was mainly &quot;a commercial decision&quot; to &quot;stay competitive&quot; and &quot;lower costs.&quot;</p>
<p>Marciano also told the Journal that union charges that Guess operates sweatshops, combined with various government investigations, are &quot;a factor as well.&quot;</p>
</text>
